  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>900</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>900</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4908a3d2-9c62-4497-b650-2e3c0c09bf47-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 132px;\" /></p><p>Electric field and electric force are related as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p>Magnetic force of a moving charge is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p>Thus, the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Using relation between magnetic and electric field, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
